Well, let's think through our method we start off with some point U plus v𝓲 that has integer coordinates and this number

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:47.809
Makes some angle off of the horizontal which I'm going to call theta

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:54.109
squaring this number the resulting angle off the horizontal is 2 times theta and

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:58.669
Of course when you project that onto the unit circle

00:12:58.950 --> 00:13:00.870
It's along the same radial line

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:07.100
